  Cell["A representation is moved to another basis with ChangeGroupRepBasis \
(v1: RepRotation). The new matrices are verified and become the active \
variant; the previous one stays stored.", "Text"], 
  Cell["ChangeGroupRepBasis[GroupTp, 6, {{0, 1}, {-1, \
0}}];\nChangeGroupRepBasis[GroupTp, 7, DiagonalMatrix[{I, -I, \
-I}]];\nChangeGroupRepBasis[Group2T, 7, DiagonalMatrix[{I, -I, -I}]];", 
   "Input", CellLabel -> "In[15]:="], Cell["Representations of the group", 
   "Section"], Cell["Names of the representations", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["Every irrep has its index (its position in the group, as in v1) and \
an automatic label: its dimension with the phases k/n of the eigenvalues \
e^{2\\[Pi]i k/n} of T. Names of your own, such as the paper's 1, 1', 2'', are \
stored in the group with SetIrrepLabels and shown by every view; they are \
saved with the group.", "Text"], Cell["The paper names the irreps of T' by \
their T phases: 1 (0), 1' (1/3), 1'' (2/3), 2 (0, 1/3), 2' (0, 2/3), 2'' \
(1/3, 2/3), 3. GroupTp was built here, so its irreps are in GAP's order; in \
that order the paper's names are:", "Text"], Cell["SetIrrepLabels[GroupTp, \
{\"1\", \"1''\", \"1'\", \"2''\", \"2'\", \"2\", \
\"3\"}];\nGroupTp[\"IrrepLabels\"]", "Input", CellLabel -> "In[16]:="], 
