form (eta and hypergeometric functions of K = 1728/j, with the coefficients \
applied) is the Expression row of ModularFormView above; \
ModularFormExpression[y2T4] returns it as data.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Evaluating a modular form", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["ModularFormEvaluate sums the q-series adaptively until the requested \
accuracy is reached, and reports the value with its estimated error (v1: \
ModularFormEva\\[Tau]). At \\[Tau] = i, q = e^{-2\\[Pi]} \\[TildeTilde] \
0.0019, so five terms already give 15 digits: the value is (0.395462, \
0.204706), as v1's five-term ModularFormIn\\[Tau] gave. v1's ModularFormEva \
result (0.398562, 0.198727) was wrong.", "Text"], 
  Cell["ModularFormEvaluate[y2T4, TauPoint[I], WorkingPrecision -> \
30][[{\"Value\", \"EstimatedError\", \"Order\"}]]", "Input", 
   CellLabel -> "In[10]:="], 
