   CellLabel -> "Out[13]="], Cell["Model building", "Section"], 
  Cell["Fields and Yukawa terms", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["Fields are created in one irrep each (v1 joined components of several \
irreps in one RepVec). The fields are v1's, by index: u = 4 + 1, d = 4 + 3, Q \
= 7, Yukawa spurions YU2 (index 6) and YU3 (7) for the up sector, YD1 (6), \
YD2 (5), YD3 (7) for the down sector. v1 named the irreps by position (1, 1', \
1'', 2, 2', 2'', 3), so its 2'' is index 6; the paper's names set above call \
index 6 the 2 (T phases 0, 1/3) and index 4 the 2''.", "Text"], 
  Cell["u12 = CreateField[GroupTp, 4, \"u\"]; u3 = CreateField[GroupTp, 1, \
\"u3\"];\nd12 = CreateField[GroupTp, 4, \"d\"]; d3 = CreateField[GroupTp, 3, \
\"d3\"];\nQ = CreateField[GroupTp, 7, \"Q\"];\nYU2 = CreateField[GroupTp, 6, \
\"YU2\"]; YU3 = CreateField[GroupTp, 7, \"YU3\"];\nYD1 = CreateField[GroupTp, \
6, \"YD1\"]; YD2 = CreateField[GroupTp, 5, \"YD2\"]; YD3 = \
CreateField[GroupTp, 7, \"YD3\"];", "Input", CellLabel -> "In[14]:="], 
  Cell["A model collects the fields; each invariant is a contraction of a \
product of fields into the trivial irrep, with one coupling per independent \
contraction (v1: GetOne, with C[i]).", "Text"], 
  Cell["up = CreateModel[GroupTp, {u12, u3, Q, YU2, YU3}];\nup = \
Fold[AddModelTerm[#1, CoupleContractions[Contractions[#1, #2]]] &, up, {{u12, \
Q, YU2}, {u12, Q, YU3}, {u3, Q, YU2}, {u3, Q, YU3}}];\nModelView[up]", 
   "Input", CellLabel -> "In[15]:="], 
